{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And they came to Marah.</b> Like לְמָרָה — a heh at the end of the word in place of a lamed at its beginning, and the tav is in place of the heh that is rooted in the word מָרָה. And in its construct state — when it is joined to the heh that he adds in place of the lamed — the heh of the root changes to tav. And so every heh that is a root in a word changes to tav in its construct state, as in ״חֵמָה אֵין לִי״ (Isaiah 27), ״וַחֲמָתוֹ בָּעֲרָה בוֹ״ (Esther 1) — the heh of the root changes to tav because it is joined to the vav that is added. And likewise ״עֶבֶד וְאָמָה״ (Leviticus 25), ״הִנֵּה אֲמָתִי בִלְהָה״ (Genesis 30), ״לְנֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה״ (Genesis 2:7), ״וְזִהֲמַתּוּ חַיָּתוֹ לָחֶם״ (Job 33), ״בֵּין הָרָמָה״ (Judges 4), ״וּתְשֻׁבָתוֹ הָרָמָתָה״ (I Samuel 7)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:35.483459756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}